A||||0||Ed||California Wildflowers||||1||
Z||000000||Ed||03-15-2000||12:30 AM||||With the sudden eruption of Spring in California, my blood is stirring to do some driving. I'm sure all of you, throughout the world, that are on this forum, have your favorites, but here's a suggestion for those of us in California, particularily the central part. <P>State Highway 25 runs south from Hollister, the earthquake capital of the west coast.  This is about an 80 mile road with NO PEOPLE. I've driven this road at times and seen about two or three cars coming my way, and I've only passed a couple.  Watch out for deer and pigs, though.  For about the next month or so, this valley should be rife with wildflowers.  Its the classic California country of John Steinbeck. <P>This road is commonly used by Road and Track to do their sports car test drives, which is how I found out about it.  They also use it as a scenic bypass to go to the Historic races in Monterey.  <P>Californians, give it try. <P>  ||||reg||1
